00:55:53,785 --> 00:55:54,818
demon lizard?

1259
00:55:54,852 --> 00:55:57,187
They didn't.
But he died anyway.

1260
00:55:57,220 --> 00:55:59,190
SERVO:
Kind of a dumb legend, really.

1261
00:55:59,223 --> 00:56:01,892
JOHNNY: It is consumed by fire.

1262
00:56:01,925 --> 00:56:03,827
But where the flames came from,
nobody knows.

1263
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:06,063
SERVO: How do you light
your own back on fire?

1264
00:56:11,068 --> 00:56:14,072
MIKE: Surprise,
it was me running the slides.

1265
00:56:14,105 --> 00:56:15,538
That's the mystery

1266
00:56:15,572 --> 00:56:17,308
and it's still a mystery...

1267
00:56:17,342 --> 00:56:19,010
After 400 years.

1268
00:56:20,978 --> 00:56:23,147
CROW: Now I'm over here.

1269
00:56:23,180 --> 00:56:24,648
I know what you're thinking.

1270
00:56:24,682 --> 00:56:26,650
SERVO: I'm boring
and my slideshow eats.

1271
00:56:26,683 --> 00:56:29,553
It's only an Indian legend,

1272
00:56:29,587 --> 00:56:31,722
part of our tribal culture.

1273
00:56:31,755 --> 00:56:33,790
Oh, I know, it's fantastic.

1274
00:56:33,823 --> 00:56:35,625
That is the one thing
that ties in

1275
00:56:35,658 --> 00:56:37,060
with what the fisherman said.

1276
00:56:37,093 --> 00:56:39,530
CROW: He said, "I got one."

1277
00:56:39,563 --> 00:56:41,732
He said the camp was attacked

1278
00:56:41,765 --> 00:56:44,335
by a lizard
that walked like a man.

1279
00:56:44,368 --> 00:56:46,003
MIKE: Michael Douglas?

1280
00:56:48,505 --> 00:56:51,042
CROW: Sheriff...

1281
00:56:51,075 --> 00:56:52,408
I want your help, Mack.

1282
00:56:52,442 --> 00:56:54,545
SERVO: My garage door opener
doesn't work.

1283
00:56:57,313 --> 00:56:59,250
CROW: Come on,
I can get a free hot lunch

1284
00:56:59,283 --> 00:57:00,685
at my kid's school.

1285
00:57:03,920 --> 00:57:07,457
Well, we've got the place
to ourselves.

1286
00:57:07,490 --> 00:57:10,628
I had them close up early
on my authority...

1287
00:57:10,662 --> 00:57:11,762
this proves something.

1288
00:57:11,795 --> 00:57:14,132
MIKE: I haven't solved
a case in years.

1289
00:57:14,165 --> 00:57:15,433
They'll know in a minute.

1290
00:57:16,600 --> 00:57:18,768
I never thought I'd see
the day when I try to solve

1291
00:57:18,802 --> 00:57:21,907
a case with Indian superstition.

1292
00:57:23,040 --> 00:57:24,508
SERVO: Johnny, you mind?

1293
00:57:24,542 --> 00:57:26,443
We are just about to find out.

1294
00:57:26,477 --> 00:57:29,613
MIKE: I am gonna beat
the stuffing out of you.

1295
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:35,185
SERVO:
Longbone goes into his windup.

1296
00:57:35,218 --> 00:57:36,187
JOHNNY: It should be

1297
00:57:37,020 --> 00:57:40,290
somewhere just about...

1298
00:57:40,323 --> 00:57:42,260
CROW: Would you finish
a sentence?

1299
00:57:42,293 --> 00:57:43,660
...here.

1300
00:57:43,693 --> 00:57:46,397
-[ Beeps ]
-What was that?

1301
00:57:46,430 --> 00:57:48,265
-I don't really know.
-MIKE: Let me make up

1302
00:57:48,298 --> 00:57:49,900
a quick legend.

1303
00:57:50,667 --> 00:57:52,403
My guess is that there's some...

1304
00:57:52,437 --> 00:57:53,770
SERVO: Peanut butter?

1305
00:57:53,803 --> 00:57:55,773
...unusual element
in this fragment

1306
00:57:55,807 --> 00:57:57,107
that synchronizes with that

1307
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:58,475
larger mass over there.

1308
00:57:58,508 --> 00:58:01,112
CROW: Oh, that's the folk mass.
They get more people.

1309
00:58:01,145 --> 00:58:03,447
Kind of produces some kind of

1310
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:04,682
energy reaction.

1311
00:58:05,748 --> 00:58:08,285
-MIKE: Let's just go eat.
-You mean this energy

1312
00:58:08,318 --> 00:58:09,553
or whatever it is

1313
00:58:10,287 --> 00:58:12,522
can turn a human into a monster?

1314
00:58:12,555 --> 00:58:13,957
SERVO: Would turn a manwich
into a meal.

1315
00:58:13,990 --> 00:58:17,293
Just like in those
werewolf tales,

1316
00:58:17,327 --> 00:58:19,630
when there's a full moon
in Transylvania?

1317
00:58:19,663 --> 00:58:22,500
Johnny, I have known you
for a long time,

1318
00:58:22,533 --> 00:58:24,067
but you got to be kidding.

1319
00:58:24,100 --> 00:58:25,235
I wish I was kidding, Mack.

1320
00:58:25,268 --> 00:58:26,870
CROW: This hair doesn't lie.

1321
00:58:26,903 --> 00:58:28,172
I'm not.

1322
00:58:28,205 --> 00:58:29,807
Now, there is an answer

1323
00:58:30,540 --> 00:58:32,042
and I think I know what it is.

1324
00:58:32,075 --> 00:58:34,645
MIKE: I copied from the Indian
sitting next to me.

1325
00:58:34,678 --> 00:58:36,680
And it makes me sick
to think about it.

1326
00:58:36,713 --> 00:58:38,782
CROW:
Soon I'll be throwing up corn,

1327
00:58:38,815 --> 00:58:42,687
green pepper, chicken, onions.

1328
00:58:44,522 --> 00:58:46,357
If what you say is true...

1329
00:58:46,390 --> 00:58:48,092
SERVO: Indians were here first?

1330
00:58:48,125 --> 00:58:49,527
...the x-rays,

1331
00:58:50,560 --> 00:58:53,130
the way the meteorite reacted

1332
00:58:54,465 --> 00:58:55,867
and your Indian legend...

1333
00:58:55,900 --> 00:58:57,835
MIKE: Is meteowrong, I'd say.

1334
00:58:57,868 --> 00:58:59,703
...and there's something
I've got to know

1335
00:58:59,737 --> 00:59:01,538
for my own peace of mind.

1336
00:59:01,572 --> 00:59:03,742
CROW: Granted,
it's a small piece.

1337
00:59:05,375 --> 00:59:06,743
JOHNNY: He's right, Paul.

1338
00:59:06,777 --> 00:59:08,545
Nobody knows what might happen.

1339
00:59:08,578 --> 00:59:10,548
SERVO: Except for Faith Popcorn.

1340
00:59:13,350 --> 00:59:15,152
Let's find out.

1341
00:59:16,153 --> 00:59:18,222
How much time do I have?

1342
00:59:18,255 --> 00:59:19,790
It'll be sundown
in half an hour.

1343
00:59:19,823 --> 00:59:21,057
MIKE: We can go to the drive-in.

1344
00:59:21,090 --> 00:59:23,493
The moon will be up
in an hour or so after then.

1345
00:59:23,527 --> 00:59:25,162
CROW: Of course,
that's just an old chubby

1346
00:59:25,195 --> 00:59:27,098
white sheriff's legend.

1347
00:59:29,100 --> 00:59:30,902
Before anything happens,

1348
00:59:31,802 --> 00:59:33,870
I wanna talk to Kathy.

1349
00:59:33,903 --> 00:59:35,972
I'm sure that can be arranged.

1350
00:59:36,005 --> 00:59:38,075
She's at the reservation,
I'll phone right now.

1351
00:59:38,108 --> 00:59:39,777
SERVO: Call me Johnny
Long-phone-her-

1352
00:59:39,810 --> 00:59:41,612
at-the-reservation-bone.

1353
00:59:43,747 --> 00:59:46,683
MIKE: Sheriff,
will you give me a sponge bath?

1354
00:59:47,918 --> 00:59:49,553
CROW: I hope they have
boiled chicken

1355
00:59:49,587 --> 00:59:51,088
and tapioca for lunch.

1356
00:59:51,122 --> 00:59:54,492
[ Buzzing ]

1357
00:59:54,525 --> 00:59:55,792
MACK:
You better give her some idea

1358
00:59:55,825 --> 00:59:57,627
of what he might have
to go through,

1359
00:59:57,660 --> 00:59:59,630
-just to prepare.
-JOHNNY: I'll try.

1360
00:59:59,663 --> 01:00:01,765
SERVO: She's not the sharpest
knife in the drawer.

1361
01:00:01,798 --> 01:00:06,503
Kathy, let me talk to you...

1362
01:00:06,537 --> 01:00:09,105
We've had to move Paul
to another room.

1363
01:00:09,138 --> 01:00:11,642
-He's in there.
-Why is he in there?

1364
01:00:11,675 --> 01:00:13,077
Why are these policemen here?

1365
01:00:13,110 --> 01:00:15,212
We're not sure
what may happen to Paul

1366
01:00:15,245 --> 01:00:16,880
after the moonrise.

1367
01:00:16,913 --> 01:00:19,250
In fact, moving him here
was his idea.

1368
01:00:19,283 --> 01:00:20,617
-But, surely...
-Kathy.

1369
01:00:20,650 --> 01:00:22,920
See, this is a hospital.

1370
01:00:22,953 --> 01:00:24,722
We can't afford
to take any chances.

1371
01:00:24,755 --> 01:00:26,657
MIKE: And we can't afford
a boom mic.

1372
01:00:26,690 --> 01:00:29,493
The moon has a strong effect
on the earth.

1373
01:00:29,527 --> 01:00:30,960
Look what it can do the tides.

1374
01:00:30,993 --> 01:00:32,963
CROW: And look
at what Tide can for stains.

1375
01:00:32,997 --> 01:00:34,898
In Paul's case,
it may trigger a whole set

1376
01:00:34,932 --> 01:00:36,967
of changes,
a temporary mutation...

1377
01:00:37,000 --> 01:00:41,405
I want to see him.
Now, please.

1378
01:00:41,438 --> 01:00:42,673
SERVO: I've known him
for eight hours.

1379
01:00:42,707 --> 01:00:44,775
I think I deserve to see him.

1380
01:00:47,910 --> 01:00:50,815
MIKE: So how's the pretending
you're not old going?

1381
01:00:54,885 --> 01:00:56,187
CROW:
His condition is so grave

1382
01:00:56,220 --> 01:00:58,890
that he's confined
to the ironing board.

1383
01:01:00,890 --> 01:01:03,928
SERVO: I see he's wearing
his Doris Day PJs.

1384
01:01:07,363 --> 01:01:09,800
CROW: I was dreaming
and then suddenly Judith Light

1385
01:01:09,833 --> 01:01:11,835
appeared over my bed.

1386
01:01:13,303 --> 01:01:15,807
SERVO: Wow, big cockroach
on the wall back there.

1387
01:01:15,840 --> 01:01:17,107
CROW: Whoo, mama.

1388
01:01:17,140 --> 01:01:20,110
[ Music playing ]

1389
01:01:23,880 --> 01:01:25,715
CROW: Nice hallway, anyway.

1390
01:01:25,748 --> 01:01:28,152
It's nearly sundown now.

1391
01:01:28,185 --> 01:01:30,720
She shouldn't be in there
much longer.

1392
01:01:30,753 --> 01:01:32,357
All right, I'll get her.

1393
01:01:33,690 --> 01:01:34,825
Kathy?

1394
01:01:34,858 --> 01:01:37,495
SERVO: Decouple and come on out.

1395
01:01:37,528 --> 01:01:38,795
Kathy.

1396
01:01:38,828 --> 01:01:40,832
MIKE: Get the hose, officer.

1397
01:01:44,702 --> 01:01:48,505
CROW: Kathy,
your skirt's on backwards.

1398
01:01:48,538 --> 01:01:51,173
-Thanks, Johnny.
-Can I take you home?

1399
01:01:51,207 --> 01:01:52,777
SERVO: As long as
you're giving it away.

1400
01:01:52,810 --> 01:01:54,712
No. Thank you, anyway.

1401
01:01:54,745 --> 01:01:55,845
It's no trouble, miss.

1402
01:01:55,878 --> 01:01:57,247
One of my men
can take you home.

1403
01:01:57,280 --> 01:01:59,015
MIKE: Guys are lining up
to take her home.

1404
01:01:59,048 --> 01:02:00,917
Thank you, captain,
I'll be all right.

1405
01:02:00,950 --> 01:02:03,820
I'd like to stay here
at the hospital.

1406
01:02:03,853 --> 01:02:05,688
CROW:
Well, I could take you there.

1407
01:02:05,722 --> 01:02:07,892
Look, I really wanna take
you somewhere.

1408
01:02:11,027 --> 01:02:15,032
MIKE: I'd almost unhook
my thumbs for her.

1409
01:02:15,065 --> 01:02:16,667
SERVO: Ladies and gentlemen,
Seth Thomas,

1410
01:02:16,700 --> 01:02:18,602
the best actor in the film.

1411
01:02:18,635 --> 01:02:22,538
[ Music playing ]

1412
01:02:22,572 --> 01:02:23,740
MIKE: There he is again.

1413
01:02:25,275 --> 01:02:27,643
How can you tell what time it
is when those little sticks

1414
01:02:27,677 --> 01:02:30,413
keep moving around like that?

1415
01:02:30,447 --> 01:02:31,415
The moon is up now.

1416
01:02:31,448 --> 01:02:33,483
I hope you're right.

1417
01:02:33,517 --> 01:02:35,185
I don't.

1418
01:02:35,218 --> 01:02:36,420
I hope I'm wrong.

1419
01:02:36,453 --> 01:02:37,653
SERVO: Johnny, let's not fight.

1420
01:02:37,687 --> 01:02:39,457
Well, we'll know
in a few minutes.

1421
01:02:40,823 --> 01:02:42,158
Something's happening.

1422
01:02:42,192 --> 01:02:44,262
-SERVO: Let me see.
-Oh, my God.

1423
01:02:46,763 --> 01:02:48,398
CROW: They leaned his bed
against the wall

1424
01:02:48,432 --> 01:02:50,300
so they could vacuum.

1425
01:02:53,035 --> 01:02:56,273
SERVO: I'm sorry,
nothing's happening. Never mind.

1426
01:02:59,577 --> 01:03:01,243
MIKE: Wow.

1427
01:03:01,277 --> 01:03:04,882
He's transforming
into the exact same person.

1428
01:03:04,915 --> 01:03:07,317
CROW: Ah, he's becoming
Michael Ontkean,

1429
01:03:07,350 --> 01:03:10,488
and then Michael Nouri,
and then Michael Parks.

1430
01:03:14,825 --> 01:03:16,627
SERVO: Ugh.

1431
01:03:16,660 --> 01:03:19,197
He's turning into Roy Scheider.

1432
01:03:23,267 --> 01:03:26,203
MIKE: I'm ready to fight
Captain Kirk.

1433
01:03:29,205 --> 01:03:31,908
SERVO: And now this from
Pond's Cold Cream.

1434
01:03:33,743 --> 01:03:35,545
Man, watching you turn
into a moon beast

1435
01:03:35,578 --> 01:03:37,482
was like watching paint dry.

1436
01:03:40,283 --> 01:03:42,585
MIKE: Are you supposed to put
your head through that hole

1437
01:03:42,618 --> 01:03:45,288
and get your picture taken?

1438
01:03:45,322 --> 01:03:46,457
Then it's true.

1439
01:03:46,490 --> 01:03:48,392
CROW: Wearing Underoos is fun.

1440
01:03:48,425 --> 01:03:49,427
It was me.

1441
01:03:50,360 --> 01:03:52,062
I killed all of those people?

1442
01:03:52,095 --> 01:03:53,563
Now it wasn't your fault, son.

1443
01:03:53,597 --> 01:03:54,832
SERVO: You're free to go.

1444
01:03:54,865 --> 01:03:56,733
They won't convict you,
they won't even blame you

1445
01:03:56,767 --> 01:03:58,168
once the people know the facts.

1446
01:03:58,202 --> 01:04:00,003
We'll soon have you back
to normal, Paul.

1447
01:04:00,037 --> 01:04:02,605
MIKE: Tomorrow we'll be
laughing about your killings.

1448
01:04:02,638 --> 01:04:04,975
-Do I need these now?
-No.

1449
01:04:05,008 --> 01:04:06,810
CROW: But, Paul, do you have
to leave your victims

1450
01:04:06,843 --> 01:04:08,177
in humorous poses?

1451
01:04:08,210 --> 01:04:11,447
Dr. Sutton has been in touch
with NASA about your case.

1452
01:04:11,480 --> 01:04:13,850
They're sending one of their
top lunar scientists

1453
01:04:13,883 --> 01:04:15,985
and one of the finest brain
surgeons in the country.

1454
01:04:16,018 --> 01:04:18,320
SERVO:
Maybe you could kill them.

1455
01:04:18,353 --> 01:04:22,425
See that particle of meteor
in the front part of your brain,

1456
01:04:22,458 --> 01:04:24,127
it's causing the problem.

1457
01:04:24,160 --> 01:04:26,763
When it's removed, you won't
have a thing to worry about.

1458
01:04:26,797 --> 01:04:29,667
You can go back to leading
your normal life.

1459
01:04:29,700 --> 01:04:31,668
MIKE: Oh, you're gonna kill me?

1460
01:04:31,702 --> 01:04:33,037
I'd like to see Kathy.

1461
01:04:33,070 --> 01:04:34,638
CROW: And I'd like to see
Marmaduke.

1462
01:04:34,672 --> 01:04:36,040
Please.

1463
01:04:36,940 --> 01:04:40,043
SERVO:
Ah, you horny serial killer you.

1464
01:04:46,015 --> 01:04:49,087
CROW: Guess what, I'm
a vicious killer, but it's okay.

1465
01:04:50,453 --> 01:04:51,888
Kathy.

1466
01:04:51,922 --> 01:04:52,890
MIKE: Ugh.

1467
01:04:54,023 --> 01:04:56,960
SERVO: Well, we'll go stand
out in the hall again.

1468
01:04:58,328 --> 01:05:01,498
MIKE: Yeah, it's boinking
guard for the losers.

1469
01:05:02,598 --> 01:05:07,103
CROW: Guests of Track
of the Moon Beast fly TWA.

1470
01:05:07,137 --> 01:05:09,205
SERVO: Does anyone
need a food cart to crap on?

1471
01:05:09,238 --> 01:05:10,540
Would you fasten
your seatbelts, please?

1472
01:05:10,573 --> 01:05:12,042
We'll be landing shortly.

1473
01:05:12,908 --> 01:05:14,678
When are we due in Albuquerque?

1474
01:05:14,712 --> 01:05:16,045
In about 20 minutes.

1475
01:05:16,078 --> 01:05:17,580
The captain got a message
a few minutes ago.

1476
01:05:17,613 --> 01:05:21,185
You and Dr. Lawrence
will be met at the airport.

1477
01:05:21,218 --> 01:05:22,585
Thank you.

1478
01:05:22,618 --> 01:05:23,920
May we get off first, please.

1479
01:05:23,953 --> 01:05:25,022
We just have some hand luggage.

1480
01:05:25,055 --> 01:05:26,388
ATTENDANT:
That's also been arranged.

1481
01:05:26,422 --> 01:05:29,292
You and Dr. Rizzo are to be
given every cooperation.

1482
01:05:29,325 --> 01:05:32,128
MIKE: I must get to my Skitch
Henderson convention.

1483
01:05:32,162 --> 01:05:34,397
I must admit, I was pretty
startled last night

1484
01:05:34,430 --> 01:05:37,133
-when I got the call.
-So was I.

1485
01:05:37,167 --> 01:05:39,802
I've never come up against
a case anything like it

1486
01:05:39,835 --> 01:05:42,772
and I've had a few unusual ones,
I must say.

1487
01:05:42,805 --> 01:05:45,975
We've been worried at NASA
all through the Apollo Program

1488
01:05:46,008 --> 01:05:49,078
about the possibility
that something

1489
01:05:49,112 --> 01:05:51,548
could cause a mutated life form.

1490
01:05:51,582 --> 01:05:53,417
Nothing ever happened.

1491
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:54,752
Until now.

1492
01:05:54,785 --> 01:05:58,655
CROW: Hey did you hear
about Niels Bohr and his wife?

1493
01:05:58,688 --> 01:06:00,823
[ Indistinct chatter ]

1494
01:06:00,857 --> 01:06:03,327
Hello, Paul, this is Dr. Rizzo.

1495
01:06:03,360 --> 01:06:04,760
-SERVO: What up, bitch?
-How are you, Paul?

1496
01:06:04,793 --> 01:06:07,965
I'm going to be operating
on you in just a little while.

1497
01:06:07,998 --> 01:06:09,767
I'm glad to see you.

1498
01:06:09,800 --> 01:06:11,400
What happens now?

1499
01:06:11,433 --> 01:06:13,337
We're going to make
another set of x-rays

1500
01:06:13,370 --> 01:06:15,538
just to check on the particle.

1501
01:06:15,572 --> 01:06:18,342
The new set will give
us an exact pinpointing

1502
01:06:18,375 --> 01:06:20,977
of the spot in the left frontal
lobe where it is.

1503
01:06:21,010 --> 01:06:23,680
MIKE: Then my doppelganger
